---
import DocsLayout from "../../layouts/DocsLayout.astro";
import { DOC_ITEMS } from "../../data/docs";

const base = import.meta.env.BASE_URL.replace(/\/$/, "");
---

<DocsLayout
  currentSlug="overview"
  title="Overview"
  description="Corvene is GitHub Desktop rewritten in Rust. Same app on the outside, no Electron on the inside."
>
  <p>
    Corvene is a rewrite of
    <a href="https://github.com/desktop/desktop/releases/tag/release-3.6.6" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GitHub Desktop 3.6.6</a>
    in Rust. The layout, menus, dialogs and shortcuts are the same, so if you know GitHub Desktop you already know
    Corvene. What's different is underneath: no Chromium, no Node. It starts in a fraction of a second and idles at
    around 50 MB.
  </p>

  <div class="note note-attention">
    <svg class="text-attention" viewBox="0 0 16 16" fill="currentColor" aria-hidden="true">
      <path d="M6.457 1.047c.659-1.234 2.427-1.234 3.086 0l6.082 11.378A1.75 1.75 0 0 1 14.082 15H1.918a1.75 1.75 0 0 1-1.543-2.575Zm1.763.707a.25.25 0 0 0-.44 0L1.698 13.132a.25.25 0 0 0 .22.368h12.164a.25.25 0 0 0 .22-.368Zm.53 3.996v2.5a.75.75 0 0 1-1.5 0v-2.5a.75.75 0 0 1 1.5 0ZM9 11a1 1 0 1 1-2 0 1 1 0 0 1 2 0Z" />
    </svg>
    <p>
      Corvene hasn't reached 1.0. macOS is the most complete. Linux works but looks slightly different in places, Windows
      is new, and Android is experimental.
    </p>
  </div>

  <h2 id="how">How it works</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>The window is drawn on the GPU by <a href="https://gpui.rs" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">GPUI</a>, the UI framework the Zed editor uses.</li>
    <li>Reading the repository (status, history, diffs) happens in process with gitoxide, so nothing has to start a <code>git</code> process for it.</li>
    <li>Anything that changes the repository runs your own <code>git</code>, so hooks, credential helpers and your config work as usual.</li>
    <li>Nothing is sent anywhere. There's no telemetry.</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="flags">Changes from GitHub Desktop</h2>
  <p>
    Corvene adds things GitHub Desktop doesn't have and fixes some of its bugs. Each of those is a
    <a href={`${base}/docs/flags`}>flag</a> you can switch off. Pick the <em>GitHub Desktop</em> preset and they all go,
    leaving you with 3.6.6 as it ships.
  </p>

  <h2 id="platforms">Platforms</h2>
  <table>
    <thead>
      <tr><th></th><th>Needs</th><th>Packages</th></tr>
    </thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td>macOS</td><td>10.15.7 on Intel, 11 on Apple Silicon</td><td>Homebrew, .dmg, .zip</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Windows</td><td>10 or 11</td><td>Installer, .msi, portable .zip</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Linux</td><td>glibc 2.35, X11 or Wayland</td><td>.deb, .rpm, AppImage, Flatpak, snap, .tar.gz</td></tr>
      <tr><td>Android</td><td>8.0</td><td>Two APKs: Corvene for phones, Corvene Legacy for tablets</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <ul>
    {DOC_ITEMS.filter((d) => d.slug !== "overview").map((d) => (
      <li>
        <a href={`${base}/docs/${d.slug}`}>{d.title}</a>: {d.description}
      </li>
    ))}
  </ul>
</DocsLayout>
